# Private memory and imports
#
# NOTE ON ANCHORING: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to THIS directory.
# `memory/store/` matches <root>/memory/store/ ONLY — it does not match
# addons/full-engine/memory/store/, which is where the full-engine code actually
# writes. Every rule protecting a path the code can create is therefore written
# with a leading `**/` so it matches at ANY depth. tests/test_private_paths_ignored.py
# derives the path list from the code's own constants and fails if this drifts.
private-memory/
private-imports/
local-memory/
vector-index/
vector-store/
**/memory/store/
memory/store/
.turbovec/
knowledge-graph/
graphify-out/
**/shared-brain.jsonl
brain/shared-brain.jsonl
# scripts/brain_archive.py moves records OUT of the brain into a sibling
# `-archive.jsonl` and leaves a `.pre-archive-<stamp>` copy of the original
# next to it. Both hold the same lesson text as the file above and neither
# name matches it, so with a brain configured inside the tree `git add -A`
# staged them in plaintext. The curated list the installer ships
# (scripts/project-os.gitignore) has carried these two rules since the
# 2026-07-26 audit; this file did not — two files, one guard (audit 2026-07-27).
**/shared-brain-archive.jsonl
**/shared-brain.jsonl.pre-archive-*
**/*.sidecar.json
**/store/*.tvim
central-brain/
**/central-brain/
.project-os-central-brain/
private-screenshots/
private-exports/
raw-exports/

